.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
# `packaging/build_deb.py --out out` and PyInstaller's generated spec. Both are build
# output of the documented .deb build, and both were missing here until a `git add -A`
# staged 480 files and an 83 MB package.
out/
# ⚠ **ANCHORED TO THE ROOT, AND THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING.** This read `truestill.spec`,
# which git matches at ANY depth - so when `(akv)` made `packaging/truestill.spec` a SOURCE file,
# `git add -A` skipped it in silence and the release lane failed with *"Spec file not found"* on
# a commit that was green everywhere else. The generated one still lands at the root when
# PyInstaller is driven by command-line flags, and that one is still build output.
/truestill.spec
build/
*.egg-info/
reports/
# Machine-local Claude Code permissions. Never tracked: it accumulates absolute paths
# and one-off command allow-rules that are meaningless outside this machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Generated by the CI dependency audit (and by running it locally); uv.lock is the source.
requirements-audit.txt
# Playwright traces/video kept from failed E2E runs, and its browser download marker.
tests/e2e/.artifacts/
# ⚠ THE JUNIT REPORT, AND ITS ABSENCE HERE TOOK DOWN A NIGHTLY. `ci.yml` writes this at the repo
# root with `--junitxml` in the `Pytest` step, and `Pytest (different collection order)` - the
# step that follows in the SAME job - then ran a whole-repo census over it. A report names every
# test it ran, and the decommissioned-layout guard in `test_layout_scheme.py` forbids strings that
# three of those test IDs spell out on purpose to prove they are rejected. So the second run read
# the first run's report and failed. Run 34681980628, 2026-09-12, on a commit whose five pushes
# were all green - that step runs on schedule and pull_request only.
#
# ⚠ **And this comment may not quote the string it is about**, which is the same guard working
# one level up: the first draft of these lines spelled it and went red on the spot.
#
# Invisible before `1867be3` widened the census from `git ls-files` to `--others`. THIS FILE IS
# THE DESIGNATED MECHANISM for "a census must not see this" - `repo_sources`'s own docstring
# says so - and a generated report was simply never added to it.
test-results.xml
# Local scratch notes and throwaway files; never tracked.
.scratch/

# Packaging-lane measurement output. Written by the rig on a runner and by anyone who runs
# packaging/time_startup.py locally - it is a reading, never a source file.
findings/
startup-work/

# Vendored exiftool, fetched and digest-verified at build time by packaging/exiftool_source.py.
# A downloaded artifact is never a source file.
exiftool-src/

# The React bundle is a build artifact, like the frozen app in dist/. It is NOT committed:
# `make frontend` builds it, and `test_the_served_bundle_was_built_from_these_sources` fails
# loudly if what is served was built from different sources.
packages/truestill-app/src/truestill_app/static/dist/
packages/truestill-app/frontend/node_modules/

# Copies of superseded files, kept for the maintainer to review and delete. Never committed.
.superseded/

# A second AI tool's per-repo configuration. It belongs to whoever is driving it, not to the
# project, and it was one `git add -A` from a commit - which is the only reason it is named here
# rather than left alone.
.cursor/
